              "end_index": 1184,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Unlike administration, a CVA is a \"debtor-in-possession\" process, with an insolvency practitioner (IP) supervising the arrangement as a Nominee, then Supervisor."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              6,
              4,
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1389,
              "end_index": 1496,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "CVAs have been notably used to renegotiate property leases, particularly in the retail and leisure sectors."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7,
              1,
              8
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1497,
              "end_index": 1681,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Creditor Engagement:** There is a reasonable expectation that creditors will agree to the proposed arrangement, as it typically offers a better return than immediate liquidation."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0,
              1
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 1682,
              "end_index": 1963,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Legal Protection from Action:** Once approved, the CVA provides legal protection, preventing unsecured creditors included in the arrangement from taking further enforcement action for pre-CVA debts, allowing the company crucial breathing space to implement a turnaround plan."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              3,
              9,
              7,
              1,
              2
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2008,
              "end_index": 2120,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Approval Threshold:** A CVA proposal requires approval by at least 75% in value of the creditors who vote."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              9,
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2121,
              "end_index": 2291,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Unconnected Creditor Veto:** A proposal will be rejected if more than 50% in value of unconnected creditors (those not associated with the company) vote against it."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              3,
              4,
              2
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2292,
              "end_index": 2489,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Secured/Preferential Creditors:** A CVA does not bind secured or preferential creditors (such as HMRC for certain tax debts since December 2020) unless they explicitly agree to the proposals."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              0,
              2
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2490,
              "end_index": 2557,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Duration:** Repayment plans usually span three to five years."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              7
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2558,
              "end_index": 2703,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Challenge Period:** Creditors may challenge the CVA within 28 days of approval on grounds of \"unfair prejudice\" or \"material irregularity.\""
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              10,
              11,
              12,
              13
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 2898,
              "end_index": 3044,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "**Moratorium (Standalone Moratorium)**\n    *   **Governing Rule:** Introduced by the **Corporate Insolvency and Governance Act 2020 (CIGA 2020)**."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              10,
              11,
              12,
              13
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3211,
              "end_index": 3343,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Directors remain in control (\"debtor-in-possession\"), but a licensed insolvency practitioner acts as a 'Monitor' to oversee affairs."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              11,
              12,
              14
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3348,
              "end_index": 3547,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Timelines/Thresholds:** Provides an initial 20 business days of protection, which can be extended for a further 20 business days by directors, or longer with creditor consent or court approval."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              11,
              12
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3754,
              "end_index": 3852,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "The company must be able to pay certain new debts and the Monitor must believe rescue is possible."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              10,
              13,
              15,
              16,
              17
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 3858,
              "end_index": 4037,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "**Restructuring Plan**\n    *   **Governing Rule:** Introduced by the **Corporate Insolvency and Governance Act 2020 (CIGA 2020)**, establishing Part 26A of the Companies Act 2006."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              10,
              13,
              17
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4205,
              "end_index": 4335,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "It can impose a plan on dissenting creditor classes, known as \"cross-class cram down,\" if the court deems it \"fair and equitable.\""
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              17
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4497,
              "end_index": 4560,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "However, the court's power of \"cram down\" can overcome dissent."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              15
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 4746,
              "end_index": 4797,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "It has been used by both SMEs and large corporates."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              18
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5170,
              "end_index": 5239,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "It imposes a moratorium, protecting the company from creditor action."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              19,
              18,
              20
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5423,
              "end_index": 5549,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "This can include a 'pre-pack administration', where a sale of the business is arranged before the administrator's appointment."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              5
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5555,
              "end_index": 5663,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "**Liquidation (Winding Up)**\n    *   **Governing Rule:** **Insolvency Act 1986** and **Companies Act 2006**."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              19,
              5,
              18
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 5928,
              "end_index": 6022,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "An IP is appointed to liquidate assets and repay creditors according to a statutory hierarchy."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              5,
              18
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 6031,
              "end_index": 6175,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "*   **Compulsory Liquidation:** Forced by creditors (or others) through a court order (winding-up petition) when a company cannot pay its debts."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              19,
              18
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 6399,
              "end_index": 6474,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "Compulsory liquidation is generally an undesirable and involuntary outcome."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              19,
              18
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 6480,
              "end_index": 6721,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "**Informal Arrangements / Restructuring**\n    *   **Detail:** This involves direct negotiations with creditors to agree on new repayment schedules or terms, such as a \"Time to Pay\" arrangement with HMRC or new terms with landlords/suppliers."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              19,
              18
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 6863,
              "end_index": 6940,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "However, it lacks legal protection from creditor action if negotiations fail."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              19
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 6946,
              "end_index": 7083,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "**Company Dissolution (Strike-Off)**\n    *   **Detail:** An administrative process to remove a company from the Companies House register."
            }
          },
          {
            "confidence_scores": null,
            "grounding_chunk_indices": [
              19,
              18,
              21
            ],
            "segment": {
              "start_index": 7260,
              "end_index": 7303,
              "part_index": null,
              "text": "It is not suitable for insolvent companies."
            }
          }
        ],
